        <title type="html"><![CDATA[TrustedTypes: Function() constructor]]></title>
        <id>https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/42462</id>
        <link href="https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/42462"/>
        <updated>2025-12-19T05:59:20.000Z</updated>
        <content type="html"><![CDATA[<img src="https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5368500?v=4" width="64" height="64" alt=""/><br/><p dir="auto">The <a href="https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/JavaScript/Reference/Global_Objects/Function/Function" rel="nofollow"><code class="notranslate">Function()</code> constructor</a> can execute its arguments as JavaScript - it is similarly dangerous as <code class="notranslate">eval()</code>.</p>
<p dir="auto">This updates the TrustedType information.<br>
