        <title type="html"><![CDATA[Fix CSS, HTML, and HTTP landing pages to match sidebar content and order]]></title>
        <id>https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/42460</id>
        <link href="https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/42460"/>
        <updated>2025-12-19T11:37:59.000Z</updated>
        <content type="html"><![CDATA[<img src="https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/23019147?u=4c0de81596ced64dc067dea5686f7ca2912db0cb&v=4" width="64" height="64" alt=""/><br/><h3 dir="auto">Description</h3>
<p dir="auto"><a class="user-mention notranslate" data-hovercard-type="user" data-hovercard-url="/users/Class/hovercard" data-octo-click="hovercard-link-click" data-octo-dimensions="link_type:self" href="https://github.com/Class">@Class</a> pointed out that our <a href="https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS#reference" rel="nofollow">CSS landing page</a>, specifically the Reference section, is missing a link to <a href="https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS/Reference/Properties" rel="nofollow">Properties</a>.</p>
<p dir="auto">I noticed a few other issues:</p>
<ul dir="auto">
<li>
<p dir="auto">CSS landing page</p>
<ul dir="auto">
<li>"Guides" and "How to" sections are missing.</li>
<li>The <a href="https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS#tools_for_css_development" rel="nofollow">Tools</a> section does not list all the tools we have in the sidebar.</li>
<li>The <a href="https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS#meta_bugs" rel="nofollow">meta bug</a> link is not needed on our landing page.</li>
</ul>
</li>
<li>
<p dir="auto"><a href="https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS/Guides" rel="nofollow">CSS guides landing page</a></p>
<ul dir="auto">
<li>The intro states that it lists guides when it actually lists modules.<br>
I've updated the text and also added how to get to the individual guides.</li>
</ul>
</li>
<li>
<p dir="auto"><a href="https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/HTML" rel="nofollow">HTML landing page</a></p>
